<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n609" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Actĭăcus</span></b> , a
		um, adj.
		Actium, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>relating to Actium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">victoria,</span>”
				<i>at Actium</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ludi,</span>”
				<i>the games which Augustus revived at Actium in honor
						of his victory</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. Tib. 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoebus, who had a temple here,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 13, 715</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acquor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					H. 15, 166</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legiones,</span>”
				<i>which had fought at Actium</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					1, 42</span></i>
			.</div>
